      "name": "Keto Stuffed Bell Peppers Recipe [Buffalo Chicken]",
      "description": "Bell peppers are such a versatile fruit! I love making stuffed peppers and anything that has a kick to it. If you are like me, this will be a weeknight dinner hit for you!\n\nThese stuffed peppers are creamy with shredded cheddar cheese, mayonnaise, and your favorite low-carb hot sauce (I always use Frank’s). This is all finished off with pungent but sharp blue cheese crumbles!\n\nRead the full recipe with full nutrition breakdown and step-by-step pictures over at:\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nIngredients:\n1 medium yellow bell pepper\n2 medium red bell pepper\nSalt and pepper to taste\n16 ounce boneless, skinless chicken breast, cooked + shredded\n2 cup cheddar cheese, shredded + divided\n3 tablespoon mayonnaise\n1/2 cup hot sauce\n3 tablespoon blue cheese\n15 ounce romaine lettuce\n\nNutrition Summary: This makes a total of 6 servings of Keto Buffalo Chicken Stuffed Peppers . Each serving comes out to be 383 calories, 23.1g fat, 5.1g net carbs, and 35.2g protein.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSee more keto recipes, knowledge and tips on the website to keep your weight loss going strong.\n\nEverything you need to know about the keto diet:\n\nGetting started? Everything you need is here:\n\nWe also make things easy with this 14 day diet plan:\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nFollow Ruled.Me for more tasty food:",
